#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Behaviour over presence, the inventory (board TI, item 4, decision D5; docs/TEST_INTEGRITY.md):
every UI test that asserts only PRESENCE, found by parsing, so the conversion (each test made to
press its control and assert the effect) can be sized and then held by a ratchet that only
shrinks, tests/presence_only.py.

    scripts/nmas-presence-inventory [--root DIR] [--all] [--controls] [--write]

**The property.** A UI test is a test function that requests a v2 page or fragment (a Flask test
client `.get(`/`.post(` on a path starting "/v2", or a real browser driven to a "/v2" URL, as the
repo's browser helpers do). It asserts PRESENCE ONLY when every assertion it makes is about a
status code, or about text/markup/an element being present or absent in the response or page,
and it never PRESSES a control and asserts the effect (no POST/PUT/DELETE through the client to a
mutating route followed by an assertion on state or a later read; no browser click/submit/
keypress followed by an assertion). Decided by parsing (`ast`): the calls made, in order; the
asserts and what they compare. Where the parse cannot decide (a helper that hides the request or
the click), the test is listed with the reason "undecided: <why>", never guessed. The first known
case: C2288's Set value…, which the commit's result drew and which did nothing when pressed
(C2331); its contract test drew the prompt and never pressed the button.

**How it is read.** Test files and test functions are nmas-test-audit-static's (`tests/**/
test_*.py`, `test_*` functions and `Test*` classes' methods; the node id without parametrize
ids), and so are its helper resolution (a function at the top of the same file, a method of the
test's class through `self.`, a name imported from `tests.`; here followed `MAX_DEPTH` levels
deep, a function defined inside the test too, each walked with its parameters bound to the
call's arguments), its fixture reading (the same file's fixtures a test names) and its status
rule (`.status_code`, `.status`, `["ok"]` and the rest, compared with constants). Each test's
body is walked statement by statement, in
order (a loop's body twice, so a press at its end comes before an assert at its start), and
every value carries what it was read from:

- **a read**: a test client's `.get/.head/.post/.put/.delete/.patch/.open` whose path is a
  string starting "/" (a literal, an f-string's leading text, a constant, a parametrize value, a
  local helper's returned string), or any such call on a receiver already seen making one in the
  file, or a client made by `.test_client()`; a browser's `.go(url)`, `.js(script)` and
  `.wait_for(script)` in a file that imports `tests.browser` (or on a receiver seen using one).
  A read's value is the response (or the page), stamped with when it was read.
- **a press**: a client request by POST, PUT, DELETE or PATCH (or `.open` with such a method);
  a browser `.click(` or `.type(`, a WebDriver `_call` to an element's click or value or to
  actions, and a `.js(`/`.wait_for(` script that clicks, submits, dispatches an event or calls
  `htmx.trigger`/`htmx.ajax`.
- **state**: anything read from the world rather than from a response: a fixture's value, a
  call to a first-party or unresolved function, a method called on a state value, a name a
  lambda or nested function passed out may change.

An assert's each `and`-ed part is then **status** (the status rule), **response** (a membership
`x in <response>`, or a value read from a response and nothing else), **mixed** (a response
compared with state, such as a drawn value with the stored one), **state** (no response in it)
or **trivial** (neither). `wait_for` is a response assert at its own time; a mock's `assert_*`
and `pytest.raises` are state asserts. Asserts made before the test's first read are its
preconditions and are not counted.

**The verdict**, per UI test:
- **pressing**: a press followed by an assert with a state or mixed part, or with a response
  part read after the press (a later read: a browser's page after a click is always one); or a
  press made after a stand-in that fails when called was passed out (`monkeypatch.setattr(job,
  "start", lambda *a: pytest.fail("started"))`), which asserts what the press does;
- **undecided: <why>**, when it would otherwise be presence-only and something it did was not
  read: the client or browser passed to a function the parse does not follow, a browser script
  that is not a string it can read, or (with no v2 read seen) a request or navigation whose
  path or URL it cannot read;
- **state**: no press asserted, but an assert after the first read on state alone (a read that
  writes nothing, a counter): not presence-only, and not a press either;
- **presence**: otherwise. Its reason says which: status only; draws only; presses but asserts
  only its own answer; or asserts nothing after its read.

**A control drawn and never pressed** (`--controls`; reported, not held by the ratchet). The
verdict is per test, so a test that presses one control and asserts its effect is pressing even
where it only draws another: C2288's own test pressed Commit and re-read the deploy offer, and
only drew the Set value… beside it, which is how that button passed (its version before C2331's
fix, c9b12114's parent, is listed by this report and called pressing by the verdict). So each
`<text> in <answer>` assert whose text names a v2 control (`hx-get|hx-post|hx-put|hx-delete|
hx-patch|action="/v2..."`) is listed when the test never requests that control's path (its
query aside). Not judged in a browser test (a click names no route) or where a request's path is
not read (it may be the press).

**What it does not see** (each a limit, never a guess): a request made through a fixture's
callable or an object's method; a request on a receiver the file never uses with a readable
path, whose own path cannot be read either (it could be any `.get`); a helper deeper than
`MAX_DEPTH` (a client or browser passed to one makes the test undecided); conftest fixtures
and fixtures imported from another file (their value is state); a test defined inside an `if`
at module level; a browser script assembled at run time from values it cannot resolve
(undecided).

**Output.** One line per presence-only and undecided test, `<verdict>\\t<test id>\\t<reason>`
(`--all` adds the pressing and state tests; `--controls` a `drawn-unpressed` line per control
drawn and never pressed), then `#` totals: UI tests scanned, presence, undecided, pressing,
state, the tests drawing a control they never press, and the test functions parsed. `--write`
writes the presence and undecided ids into `<root>/tests/presence_only.py` (`PRESENCE_ONLY`,
`UNDECIDED`), the list tests/test_presence_only.py holds and tests/ratchet_lists.py declares
`shrinks`. Exit 0; 2 for a root with no `tests/`.
"""
import argparse
import ast
import collections
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import os
import re
import sys

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
REPO = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
sys.path.insert(0, REPO)
# Phase 4 section 8.1: the interpreter flask-app runs, before any other import.
from modules.app_interpreter import adopt  # noqa: E402
adopt(__name__)


def _load(name):
    path = os.path.join(REPO, "scripts", name)
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(name.replace("-", "_"), path)
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader(loader.name, loader))
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


#: The existing-test audit's static tool: its test files, test functions, helper and fixture
#: resolution and status rule are this inventory's, never a second copy.
S = _load("nmas-test-audit-static")


_INFOS = {}


def _info_once(cls):
    """The tool's `imported` builds the imported file's FileInfo at every call (8,288 of them a
    scan, 76 s of its 122, profiled 2026-11-03); here each file's is built once, in this
    process's copy of the tool only (cleared with the tool's own caches by `inventory`)."""
    def make(root, path, tree):
        key = (root, path)
        if key not in _INFOS:
            _INFOS[key] = cls(root, path, tree)
        return _INFOS[key]
    return make


S.FileInfo = _info_once(S.FileInfo)

REQUEST_METHODS = {"get", "head", "post", "put", "delete", "patch", "open"}
MUTATING = {"post", "put", "delete", "patch"}
BROWSER_METHODS = {"go", "click", "type", "js", "wait_for", "_call"}
#: A browser script that presses: a click, a submit, a dispatched event, an htmx trigger.
PRESS_SCRIPT = re.compile(r"\.click\(\s*\)|dispatchEvent\s*\(|requestSubmit\s*\(|"
                          r"\.submit\(\s*\)|htmx\.trigger\s*\(|htmx\.ajax\s*\(")
#: A raw WebDriver command that presses (an element's click or keys, or an action chain).
WEBDRIVER_PRESS = re.compile(r"/click\b|/value\b|/actions\b")
#: A v2 control an assert's text says is drawn: htmx's request attributes and a form's action.
DRAWN_CONTROL = re.compile(r'(?:hx-(?:get|post|put|delete|patch)|action)="(/v2[^"]*)"')
PURE_BUILTINS = {
    "abs", "all", "any", "bool", "bytes", "chr", "dict", "divmod", "enumerate", "filter",
    "float", "format", "frozenset", "hash", "int", "isinstance", "issubclass", "iter", "len",
    "list", "map", "max", "min", "next", "ord", "range", "repr", "reversed", "round", "set",
    "sorted", "str", "sum", "tuple", "type", "zip"}
#: Modules whose functions compute from their arguments alone (parsing, matching, formatting).
PURE_MODULES = {"re", "json", "html", "textwrap", "urllib", "urllib.parse", "bs4", "string",
                "itertools", "functools", "collections", "math", "base64", "hashlib", "shlex",
                "difflib", "ast", "copy", "html.parser", "operator", "unicodedata"}
UNKNOWN = "\x00"            # an unresolved part of a string
MAX_STRINGS = 64
#: How many helper levels are followed (a test's helper, and that helper's own).
MAX_DEPTH = 2


class Taint:
    """What a value was read from: a response (the latest read time) and/or the world."""
    __slots__ = ("resp", "state")

    def __init__(self, resp=None, state=False):
        self.resp, self.state = resp, state

    def __or__(self, other):
        r = [x for x in (self.resp, other.resp) if x is not None]
        return Taint(max(r) if r else None, self.state or other.state)


PURE = Taint()
WORLD = Taint(state=True)


def union(taints):
    out = Taint()
    for t in taints:
        out = out | t
    return out


# --- the file's own facts --------------------------------------------------------------------

def imports_browser(n):
    """An import of the repo's browser helper, tests/browser.py."""
    if isinstance(n, ast.ImportFrom) and n.module:
        return n.module == "tests.browser" or (n.module == "tests" and
                                               any(a.name == "browser" for a in n.names))
    return isinstance(n, ast.Import) and any(a.name == "tests.browser" for a in n.names)


def literal_path(node):
    """A request's path when it is written out: a string or an f-string's leading text."""
    if isinstance(node, ast.Constant) and isinstance(node.value, str):
        return node.value
    if isinstance(node, ast.JoinedStr) and node.values and \
            isinstance(node.values[0], ast.Constant):
        return node.values[0].value
    return None


def path_arg(call):
    if call.args:
        return call.args[0]
    for k in call.keywords:
        if k.arg in ("path", "url"):
            return k.value
    return None


class FileFacts:
    """One test file: the audit tool's FileInfo, its module constants, and the receivers it
    uses as a client and as a browser."""
    _cache = {}

    @classmethod
    def of(cls, root, path):
        key = (root, path)
        if key not in cls._cache:
            tree = S.parse(path)
            cls._cache[key] = cls(root, path, tree) if tree is not None else None
        return cls._cache[key]

    def __init__(self, root, path, tree):
        self.root, self.path, self.tree = root, path, tree
        self.info = S.FileInfo(root, path, tree)
        self.browser = False
        self.consts = {}
        self._strings = {}          # module constant -> its strings, read once
        self.literals = set()       # names bound to a collection display: data, not a client
        for n in tree.body:
            targets = n.targets if isinstance(n, ast.Assign) else \
                [n.target] if isinstance(n, ast.AnnAssign) and n.value is not None else []
            for t in targets:
                if isinstance(t, ast.Name):
                    self.consts[t.id] = n.value
                    if isinstance(n.value, (ast.Dict, ast.List, ast.Tuple, ast.Set)):
                        self.literals.add(t.id)
        # One walk: the browser helper's import, the receivers of requests with a written-out
        # path, the receivers of the browser's methods, and names bound to `.test_client()`.
        clients, browser_calls = [], []
        for n in ast.walk(tree):
            if isinstance(n, (ast.Import, ast.ImportFrom)) and imports_browser(n):
                self.browser = True
            elif isinstance(n, ast.Call) and isinstance(n.func, ast.Attribute):
                if n.func.attr in REQUEST_METHODS:
                    p = path_arg(n)
                    lit = literal_path(p) if p is not None else None
                    if lit is not None and lit.startswith("/") and \
                            not self.is_data(n.func.value):
                        clients.append(n.func.value)
                elif n.func.attr in BROWSER_METHODS:
                    browser_calls.append(n.func.value)
            elif isinstance(n, (ast.Assign, ast.withitem)):
                value = n.value if isinstance(n, ast.Assign) else n.context_expr
                targets = n.targets if isinstance(n, ast.Assign) else \
                    [n.optional_vars] if n.optional_vars is not None else []
                if isinstance(value, ast.Call) and S.call_name(value) == "test_client":
                    clients += targets
        self.client_handles = {handle_key(e) for e in clients}
        self.browser_handles = {handle_key(e) for e in browser_calls} if self.browser else set()

    def is_data(self, expr):
        return isinstance(expr, ast.Name) and expr.id in self.literals

    def module_strings(self, name, seen):
        """A module constant's strings, or one imported by name from another `tests.` file."""
        key = (self.path, name)
        if key in seen:
            return None
        if name in self._strings:
            return self._strings[name]
        got = None
        node = self.consts.get(name)
        if node is not None:
            got = strings(node, Scope(self), seen | {key})
        elif name in self.info.from_names:
            mod, orig = self.info.from_names[name]
            path = S.module_file(self.root, mod) if mod.split(".")[0] == "tests" else None
            other = FileFacts.of(self.root, path) if path else None
            if other is not None and other is not self:
                got = other.module_strings(orig, seen | {key})
        if not seen:                # a value read inside a cycle's guard is not kept
            self._strings[name] = got
        return got


_CTX = re.compile(r", ctx=(?:Load|Store|Del)\(\)")


def _norm(dump):
    """A dump without its load/store context, so `b` bound and `b` used compare equal."""
    return _CTX.sub("", dump)


def handle_key(expr):
    """An expression's identity as a receiver: its dump without context (a bare name built
    directly, the dump's own spelling, since most receivers are one)."""
    if isinstance(expr, ast.Name):
        return f"Name(id={expr.id!r})"
    if isinstance(expr, (ast.Constant, ast.Lambda, ast.JoinedStr)):
        return ""               # never a client or a browser
    return _norm(ast.dump(expr))


# --- strings: what a path, a URL or a script can be ------------------------------------------

class Scope:
    """Names a string can be resolved through: the frame's own, then the class's, then the
    module's constants."""

    def __init__(self, facts, local=None, classes=()):
        self.facts, self.local, self.classes = facts, local or {}, classes

    def lookup(self, name, seen):
        if name in self.local:
            return self.local[name]
        return self.facts.module_strings(name, seen)

    def class_attr(self, attr, seen):
        for cls in reversed(self.classes):
            for n in cls.body:
                if isinstance(n, ast.Assign) and any(
                        isinstance(t, ast.Name) and t.id == attr for t in n.targets):
                    return strings(n.value, Scope(self.facts), seen | {"self." + attr})
        return None


def _product(a, b):
    out = [x + y for x in a for y in b]
    return out[:MAX_STRINGS]


def strings(node, scope, seen=frozenset()):
    """The strings *node* may be, an unresolved part written UNKNOWN; None when nothing of it
    can be read."""
    if isinstance(node, ast.Constant):
        if isinstance(node.value, str):
            return [node.value]
        if isinstance(node.value, (int, float)) and not isinstance(node.value, bool):
            return [str(node.value)]        # a width or a count written into a script
        return None
    if isinstance(node, ast.JoinedStr):
        out = [""]
        for v in node.values:
            if isinstance(v, ast.Constant):
                out = _product(out, [str(v.value)])
            else:
                part = strings(v.value, scope, seen) if isinstance(v, ast.FormattedValue) \
                    else None
                out = _product(out, part or [UNKNOWN])
        return out
    if isinstance(node, ast.BinOp) and isinstance(node.op, ast.Add):
        left, right = strings(node.left, scope, seen), strings(node.right, scope, seen)
        if left is None and right is None:
            return None
        return _product(left or [UNKNOWN], right or [UNKNOWN])
    if isinstance(node, ast.BinOp) and isinstance(node.op, ast.Mod):
        # `"..%d.." % X`: the text and what is put into it (its place in the text aside).
        left = strings(node.left, scope, seen)
        return _product(left, strings(node.right, scope, seen) or [UNKNOWN]) if left else None
    if isinstance(node, ast.Name):
        return scope.lookup(node.id, seen)
    if isinstance(node, ast.Attribute) and isinstance(node.value, ast.Name) and \
            node.value.id in ("self", "cls"):
        return scope.class_attr(node.attr, seen)
    if isinstance(node, ast.Subscript):
        return strings(node.value, scope, seen)
    if isinstance(node, (ast.Tuple, ast.List, ast.Set)):
        out = []
        for e in node.elts:
            out += strings(e, scope, seen) or []
        return out[:MAX_STRINGS] if out else None
    if isinstance(node, ast.Dict):
        out = []
        for e in list(node.keys) + list(node.values):
            out += (strings(e, scope, seen) or []) if e is not None else []
        return out[:MAX_STRINGS] if out else None
    if isinstance(node, ast.IfExp):
        out = (strings(node.body, scope, seen) or []) + (strings(node.orelse, scope, seen) or [])
        return out or None
    if isinstance(node, ast.Call):
        f = node.func
        if isinstance(f, ast.Attribute) and f.attr in ("format", "replace", "strip", "lower",
                                                       "rstrip", "lstrip", "upper"):
            base = strings(f.value, scope, seen)
            return [s + (UNKNOWN if f.attr == "format" else "") for s in base] if base else None
        if isinstance(f, ast.Attribute) and f.attr in ("items", "values", "keys", "get"):
            return strings(f.value, scope, seen)    # a mapping's strings, keys and values
        if isinstance(f, ast.Name) and f.id in ("str", "sorted", "list", "tuple", "set") and \
                node.args:
            return strings(node.args[0], scope, seen)
        if isinstance(f, ast.Name) and f.id in scope.facts.info.funcs and f.id not in seen:
            return helper_strings(scope.facts.info.funcs[f.id], node, scope, seen | {f.id})
    return None


def helper_strings(fn, call, scope, seen):
    """The strings a local helper returns, its parameters bound to the call's arguments."""
    params = [a.arg for a in fn.args.args]
    local = {}
    for p, a in zip(params, call.args):
        local[p] = strings(a, scope, seen)
    for k in call.keywords:
        if k.arg:
            local[k.arg] = strings(k.value, scope, seen)
    inner = Scope(scope.facts, {k: v for k, v in local.items() if v is not None})
    if id(fn) not in _RETURNS:
        _RETURNS[id(fn)] = [n.value for n in ast.walk(fn)
                            if isinstance(n, ast.Return) and n.value is not None]
    out = []
    for value in _RETURNS[id(fn)]:
        out += strings(value, inner, seen) or []
    return out[:MAX_STRINGS] or None


#: id(function node) -> its returned expressions (the trees live as long as the tool's cache).
_RETURNS = {}


def deep_strings(node, scope):
    """Every string inside *node*'s subtree that resolves, and whether every leaf did."""
    whole = strings(node, scope)
    if whole is not None:
        return whole, all(UNKNOWN not in s for s in whole)
    out = []        # the whole did not resolve (a call such as `srv.url(x)`): its parts
    for sub in ast.walk(node):
        if sub is node:
            continue
        got = strings(sub, scope) if isinstance(sub, (ast.Constant, ast.Name, ast.JoinedStr,
                                                      ast.BinOp, ast.Attribute)) else None
        if got:
            out += got
    return out, False


# --- one test, walked in order ---------------------------------------------------------------

class Run:
    """The events of one test: reads, presses, asserts and what was not read."""

    def __init__(self, root, facts):
        self.root, self.facts = root, facts
        self.clock = 0
        self.reads, self.presses, self.asserts, self.unread = [], [], [], []
        #: (time, where): a stand-in passed out that fails when called (`lambda:
        #: pytest.fail("started")`), an assert on what any later press does.
        self.traps = []
        #: (control's path, where): a v2 control an assert says is drawn (`hx-get="/v2/..."`).
        self.drawn = []
        self.v2_seen = False

    def marks(self):
        return (self.clock, len(self.reads), len(self.presses), len(self.asserts),
                len(self.unread), len(self.traps), len(self.drawn))

    def rewind(self, saved):
        self.clock = saved[0]
        del self.reads[saved[1]:], self.presses[saved[2]:], self.asserts[saved[3]:]
        del self.unread[saved[4]:], self.traps[saved[5]:], self.drawn[saved[6]:]

    def tick(self):
        self.clock += 1
        return self.clock


class Frame:
    def __init__(self, run, facts, classes, depth, local_strings=None):
        self.run, self.facts, self.classes, self.depth = run, facts, classes, depth
        # The receivers used as a client and as a browser: the file's, and this frame's own
        # (a helper's parameter given one), kept per frame so no test's walk changes another's.
        self.clients, self.browsers = set(facts.client_handles), set(facts.browser_handles)
        self.env = {}
        self.local_strings = dict(local_strings or {})
        self.local_defs = {}
        self.returns = []

    @property
    def scope(self):
        return Scope(self.facts, self.local_strings, self.classes)

    def where(self, lineno):
        """`line N` in the test's own file, `<file>:N` in a helper's."""
        if self.facts is self.run.facts:
            return f"line {lineno}"
        return f"{S.rel(self.run.root, self.facts.path)}:{lineno}"

    # -- statements --

    def walk(self, body):
        for stmt in body:
            self.stmt(stmt)

    def bind(self, target, taint, strs=None):
        if isinstance(target, ast.Name):
            self.env[target.id] = taint
            if strs is not None:
                self.local_strings[target.id] = strs
            else:
                self.local_strings.pop(target.id, None)
        elif isinstance(target, (ast.Tuple, ast.List)):
            for e in target.elts:
                self.bind(e.value if isinstance(e, ast.Starred) else e, taint, strs)
        elif isinstance(target, (ast.Attribute, ast.Subscript)):
            self.expr(target.value)
            base = target.value
            if isinstance(base, ast.Name) and base.id in self.env:   # `found[k] = v`
                self.env[base.id] = self.env[base.id] | taint

    def stmt(self, s):
        run = self.run
        if isinstance(s, ast.Expr):
            self.expr(s.value)
        elif isinstance(s, (ast.Assign, ast.AnnAssign)):
            if s.value is None:
                return
            t = self.expr(s.value)
            strs = strings(s.value, self.scope)
            for target in (s.targets if isinstance(s, ast.Assign) else [s.target]):
                self.bind(target, t, strs)
        elif isinstance(s, ast.AugAssign):
            t = self.expr(s.value)
            if isinstance(s.target, ast.Name):
                self.env[s.target.id] = self.env.get(s.target.id, PURE) | t
        elif isinstance(s, ast.Assert):
            self.assertion(s)
        elif isinstance(s, (ast.If, ast.While)):
            self.expr(s.test)
            for _ in range(2 if isinstance(s, ast.While) else 1):
                self.walk(s.body)
            self.walk(s.orelse)
        elif isinstance(s, (ast.For, ast.AsyncFor)):
            t = self.expr(s.iter)
            self.bind(s.target, t, strings(s.iter, self.scope))
            self.walk(s.body)
            self.walk(s.body)
            self.walk(s.orelse)
        elif isinstance(s, (ast.With, ast.AsyncWith)):
            raises = False
            for item in s.items:
                c = item.context_expr
                if isinstance(c, ast.Call) and self._is_raises(c):
                    raises = True
                t = self.expr(c)
                if item.optional_vars is not None:
                    self.bind(item.optional_vars, t)
            self.walk(s.body)
            if raises:
                run.asserts.append((run.tick(), [("state", None)], self.where(s.lineno)))
        elif isinstance(s, ast.Try) or type(s).__name__ == "TryStar":
            self.walk(s.body)
            for h in s.handlers:
                if h.name:
                    self.env[h.name] = WORLD
                self.walk(h.body)
            self.walk(s.orelse)
            self.walk(s.finalbody)
        elif isinstance(s, ast.Return):
            if s.value is not None:
                self.returns.append(self.expr(s.value))
        elif isinstance(s, (ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef)):
            self.local_defs[s.name] = s
            self.passed_out(s)
        elif isinstance(s, ast.ClassDef):
            self.passed_out(s)
        elif hasattr(ast, "Match") and isinstance(s, ast.Match):
            self.expr(s.subject)
            for case in s.cases:
                self.walk(case.body)

    def _is_raises(self, call):
        f = call.func
        names = self.facts.info.pytest_names
        if isinstance(f, ast.Attribute) and f.attr in ("raises", "warns") and \
                isinstance(f.value, ast.Name) and f.value.id in names["module"]:
            return True
        return isinstance(f, ast.Name) and f.id in names["direct"]

    def passed_out(self, node):
        """A closure may change the names it reads: each becomes state."""
        for n in ast.walk(node):
            if isinstance(n, ast.Name) and n.id in self.env:
                self.env[n.id] = self.env[n.id] | WORLD

    # -- asserts --

    def assertion(self, s):
        parts = []
        conjuncts = s.test.values if isinstance(s.test, ast.BoolOp) and \
            isinstance(s.test.op, ast.And) else [s.test]
        for c in conjuncts:
            t = self.expr(c)
            self._drawn_controls(c, s.lineno)
            if S.status_conjunct(c):
                parts.append(("status", t.resp))
            elif self._membership_in_response(c):
                parts.append(("response", t.resp))
            elif t.resp is not None and t.state:
                parts.append(("mixed", t.resp))
            elif t.resp is not None:
                parts.append(("response", t.resp))
            elif t.state:
                parts.append(("state", None))
            else:
                parts.append(("trivial", None))
        self.run.asserts.append((self.run.tick(), parts, self.where(s.lineno)))

    def _membership_in_response(self, c):
        if not isinstance(c, ast.Compare) or not all(isinstance(op, (ast.In, ast.NotIn))
                                                     for op in c.ops):
            return False
        return union(self.expr_quiet(x) for x in c.comparators).resp is not None

    def _drawn_controls(self, c, lineno):
        """`'hx-get="/v2/..."' in html`: a control the assert says is drawn (C2288's shape)."""
        if not (isinstance(c, ast.Compare) and len(c.ops) == 1 and isinstance(c.ops[0], ast.In)):
            return
        for s in strings(c.left, self.scope) or []:
            for m in DRAWN_CONTROL.finditer(s):
                self.run.drawn.append((m.group(1).replace("&amp;", "&"), self.where(lineno)))

    # -- expressions --

    def name(self, n):
        if n in self.env:
            return self.env[n]
        info = self.facts.info
        if n in self.facts.consts:
            return PURE
        if n in info.from_names or n in info.module_alias:
            mod = info.module_alias.get(n) or info.from_names[n][0]
            return PURE if mod in PURE_MODULES or mod.split(".")[0] in PURE_MODULES else WORLD
        if n in PURE_BUILTINS or n in ("True", "False", "None"):
            return PURE
        return WORLD

    def expr(self, e):
        if e is None:
            return PURE
        if isinstance(e, ast.Constant):
            return PURE
        if isinstance(e, ast.Name):
            return self.name(e.id)
        if isinstance(e, ast.Call):
            return self.call(e)
        if isinstance(e, ast.Lambda):
            self.passed_out(e)
            return PURE
        if isinstance(e, (ast.ListComp, ast.SetComp, ast.GeneratorExp, ast.DictComp)):
            saved = dict(self.env)
            out = PURE
            for g in e.generators:
                it = self.expr(g.iter)
                out = out | it
                self.bind(g.target, it)
                for cond in g.ifs:
                    out = out | self.expr(cond)
            if isinstance(e, ast.DictComp):
                out = out | self.expr(e.key) | self.expr(e.value)
            else:
                out = out | self.expr(e.elt)
            self.env = saved
            return out
        if isinstance(e, ast.NamedExpr):
            t = self.expr(e.value)
            self.bind(e.target, t, strings(e.value, self.scope))
            return t
        if isinstance(e, (ast.Yield, ast.YieldFrom)):
            t = self.expr(e.value)
            self.returns.append(t)
            return PURE
        out = PURE
        for child in ast.iter_child_nodes(e):
            if isinstance(child, ast.expr):
                out = out | self.expr(child)
            elif isinstance(child, ast.comprehension):
                out = out | self.expr(child.iter)
        return out

    def call(self, c):
        f = c.func
        run, facts = self.run, self.facts
        recv = self.expr(f.value) if isinstance(f, ast.Attribute) else PURE
        args = [self.expr(a.value if isinstance(a, ast.Starred) else a) for a in c.args]
        args += [self.expr(k.value) for k in c.keywords]
        attr = f.attr if isinstance(f, ast.Attribute) else None
        if attr is not None and isinstance(f.value, ast.Name) and f.value.id in self.env:
            # `problems.append(x)`: a local's method may keep what it is given.
            self.env[f.value.id] = self.env[f.value.id] | union(args)

        if attr in REQUEST_METHODS:
            got = self.request(c, attr)
            if got is not None:
                return got
        if attr in BROWSER_METHODS and (facts.browser or handle_key(f.value)
                                        in self.browsers):
            return self.browser(c, attr)
        if attr == "emit" and handle_key(f.value) in self.clients:
            run.presses.append((run.tick(), f"emit {ast.unparse(c.args[0])[:40]}"
                                if c.args else "emit"))
            return PURE
        if attr is not None and attr.startswith("assert"):
            t = recv | union(args)
            run.asserts.append((run.tick(), [("response", t.resp) if t.resp is not None
                                             else ("state", None)], self.where(c.lineno)))
            return PURE
        if self._is_raises(c) and len(c.args) >= 2:
            run.asserts.append((run.tick(), [("state", None)], self.where(c.lineno)))
            return WORLD
        # A helper, its parameters bound to the call's arguments.
        if self.depth < MAX_DEPTH:
            target = None
            if isinstance(f, ast.Name) and f.id in self.local_defs:
                target = (self.local_defs[f.id], facts, self.classes, False)
            else:
                for _k, _n, node, hinfo in S.helper_targets(c, facts.info, self.classes):
                    hf = FileFacts.of(self.run.root, hinfo.path) if hinfo.path != facts.path \
                        else facts
                    if hf is not None:
                        target = (node, hf, self.classes if hf is facts else (),
                                  isinstance(f, ast.Attribute) and isinstance(f.value, ast.Name)
                                  and f.value.id == "self")
                    break
            if target is not None:
                return self.splice(c, args, *target)
        # Anything else: a pure computation, or a read of the world.
        if self._pure(c, recv):
            return recv | union(args)
        self._handles_passed(c)
        self._traps(c)
        run.tick()
        return recv | union(args) | WORLD

    def _pure(self, c, recv):
        """Whether the call computes from what it is given (*recv*: its receiver's taint)."""
        f, info = c.func, self.facts.info
        if isinstance(f, ast.Name):
            if f.id in self.env or f.id in self.local_defs:
                return False
            if f.id in PURE_BUILTINS:
                return True
            if f.id in info.from_names:
                mod = info.from_names[f.id][0]
                return mod in PURE_MODULES or mod.split(".")[0] in PURE_MODULES
            return False
        if isinstance(f, ast.Attribute):
            mod = info.dotted(f.value)
            if mod is not None:
                return mod in PURE_MODULES or mod.split(".")[0] in PURE_MODULES
            base = f.value
            if isinstance(base, ast.Name) and base.id in info.from_names and \
                    base.id not in self.env:
                mod = info.from_names[base.id][0]
                return mod in PURE_MODULES or mod.split(".")[0] in PURE_MODULES
            # A method of a value: pure on a response or a constant, a read on state.
            return not recv.state
        return False

    def expr_quiet(self, e):
        """A value's taint, the events its evaluation would add left out (read twice)."""
        saved = self.run.marks()
        t = self.expr(e)
        self.run.rewind(saved)
        return t

    def _traps(self, c):
        """A stand-in passed out that fails when called asserts what a later press does."""
        names = self.facts.info.pytest_names
        for a in list(c.args) + [k.value for k in c.keywords]:
            node = a if isinstance(a, ast.Lambda) else \
                self.local_defs.get(a.id) if isinstance(a, ast.Name) else None
            if node is not None and S.asserting_nodes(ast.walk(node), names):
                self.run.traps.append((self.run.tick(), self.where(a.lineno)))

    def _handles_passed(self, c):
        handles = self.clients | self.browsers
        for a in list(c.args) + [k.value for k in c.keywords]:
            if isinstance(a, ast.Starred):
                a = a.value
            if handle_key(a) in handles:
                self.run.unread.append(f"the client or browser `{ast.unparse(a)}` is passed to "
                                       f"`{S.short(ast.unparse(c.func), 50)}`, which the parse "
                                       "does not follow")
                return

    def splice(self, c, taints, node, hfacts, classes, is_method):
        """A helper walked in place, its parameters bound to the call's arguments (*taints*,
        already evaluated: the positional ones, then the keywords)."""
        params = [a.arg for a in node.args.args]
        if is_method and params:
            params = params[1:]
        frame = Frame(self.run, hfacts, classes, self.depth + 1)
        defaults = node.args.defaults
        for p, d in zip(params[len(params) - len(defaults):], defaults):
            frame.env[p] = PURE
            s = strings(d, frame.scope)
            if s is not None:
                frame.local_strings[p] = s
        for p in params:
            frame.env.setdefault(p, WORLD)
        if is_method and node.args.args:
            frame.env[node.args.args[0].arg] = WORLD
        scope = self.scope
        positional = list(zip(params, zip(c.args, taints)))
        keywords = [(k.arg, (k.value, t)) for k, t in zip(c.keywords, taints[len(c.args):])
                    if k.arg]
        for p, (a, t) in positional + keywords:
            if isinstance(a, ast.Starred):
                continue
            frame.env[p] = t
            s = strings(a, scope)
            if s is not None:
                frame.local_strings[p] = s
            if handle_key(a) in self.clients:
                frame.clients.add(handle_key(ast.Name(id=p)))
            if handle_key(a) in self.browsers:
                frame.browsers.add(handle_key(ast.Name(id=p)))
        frame.walk(node.body)
        return union(frame.returns) if frame.returns else PURE

    # -- reads and presses --

    def request(self, c, method):
        run, facts = self.run, self.facts
        p = path_arg(c)
        recv = c.func.value
        strs = strings(p, self.scope) if p is not None else None
        known = handle_key(recv) in self.clients and strs is None
        paths = [s for s in strs or [] if s.startswith("/")]
        if facts.is_data(recv) or not (paths or known):
            return None
        if method == "open":
            for k in c.keywords:
                if k.arg == "method" and isinstance(k.value, ast.Constant):
                    method = str(k.value.value).lower()
            method = method if method in REQUEST_METHODS - {"open"} else "get"
        v2 = any(s.startswith("/v2") for s in paths) if paths else None
        shown = (paths[0].replace(UNKNOWN, "{…}") if paths else
                 S.short(ast.unparse(p), 40) if p is not None else "?")
        t = run.tick()
        run.reads.append((t, method.upper(), shown, v2, "client"))
        if v2:
            run.v2_seen = True
        if method in MUTATING:
            run.presses.append((t, f"{method.upper()} {shown}"))
        self.clients.add(handle_key(recv))
        return Taint(resp=t)

    def browser(self, c, attr):
        run, facts = self.run, self.facts
        self.browsers.add(handle_key(c.func.value))
        scope = self.scope
        if attr == "go":
            arg = path_arg(c)
            strs, complete = deep_strings(arg, scope) if arg is not None else ([], False)
            v2 = True if any("/v2" in s for s in strs) else (False if complete else None)
            shown = next((s for s in strs if "/v2" in s), None) or \
                (S.short(ast.unparse(arg), 40) if arg is not None else "?")
            t = run.tick()
            run.reads.append((t, "GO", shown.replace(UNKNOWN, "{…}"), v2, "browser"))
            if v2:
                run.v2_seen = True
            return PURE
        if attr in ("click", "type"):
            css = S.short(ast.unparse(c.args[0]), 40) if c.args else "?"
            run.presses.append((run.tick(), f"{attr} {css}"))
            return PURE
        if attr == "_call":
            text = " ".join(s for a in c.args for s in deep_strings(a, scope)[0])
            if WEBDRIVER_PRESS.search(text):
                run.presses.append((run.tick(), "WebDriver " + WEBDRIVER_PRESS.search(text)[0]))
            elif "/url" in text and len(c.args) >= 3:
                strs, complete = deep_strings(c.args[2], scope)
                v2 = True if any("/v2" in s for s in strs) else (False if complete else None)
                t = run.tick()
                run.reads.append((t, "GO", "WebDriver url", v2, "browser"))
                if v2:
                    run.v2_seen = True
            return PURE
        # js / wait_for: the page read now, and a press when the script presses.
        script = c.args[0] if c.args else None
        strs = strings(script, scope) if script is not None else None
        text = " ".join(strs or [])
        t = run.tick()
        if PRESS_SCRIPT.search(text):
            run.presses.append((t, f"{attr} script {PRESS_SCRIPT.search(text)[0].strip()}"))
        elif strs is None or UNKNOWN in text:
            run.unread.append(f"a browser script that is not read: "
                              f"`{S.short(ast.unparse(script), 50) if script else '?'}`")
        if attr == "wait_for":
            t = run.tick()
            run.asserts.append((t, [("response", t)], self.where(c.lineno)))
            return Taint(resp=t)
        return Taint(resp=t)


# --- the verdict -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

def parametrized(func, classes, facts):
    """name -> the strings a parametrize decorator gives it (the function's and its classes')."""
    out = {}
    for holder in list(classes) + [func]:
        for d in holder.decorator_list:
            if not (isinstance(d, ast.Call) and S.call_name(d) == "parametrize" and
                    len(d.args) >= 2):
                continue
            names = strings(d.args[0], Scope(facts)) or []
            names = [n.strip() for s in names for n in s.split(",") if n.strip()]
            values = d.args[1]
            if isinstance(values, ast.Name):
                values = facts.consts.get(values.id, values)
            per = collections.defaultdict(list)
            if isinstance(values, (ast.List, ast.Tuple)):
                for el in values.elts:
                    if isinstance(el, ast.Call) and S.call_name(el) == "param":
                        el = ast.Tuple(elts=el.args) if len(names) > 1 else \
                            (el.args[0] if el.args else el)
                    if len(names) > 1 and isinstance(el, (ast.Tuple, ast.List)):
                        for n, v in zip(names, el.elts):
                            per[n] += strings(v, Scope(facts)) or []
                    elif names:
                        per[names[0]] += strings(el, Scope(facts)) or []
            else:
                got = strings(values, Scope(facts)) or []
                for n in names:
                    per[n] += got
            for n in names:
                out[n] = per.get(n, [])
    return out


def judge(root, facts, chain, classes, func):
    """(verdict, reason) for one test function, or None when it is not a UI test."""
    run = Run(root, facts)
    frame = Frame(run, facts, classes, 0)
    params = parametrized(func, classes, facts)
    named, _auto = S.fixtures_of(facts.info, classes)
    for a in func.args.args + func.args.kwonlyargs:
        if a.arg in params:
            frame.env[a.arg] = PURE
            frame.local_strings[a.arg] = params[a.arg]
        elif a.arg in named:
            fx = Frame(run, facts, classes, 1)
            for b in named[a.arg].args.args:
                fx.env[b.arg] = WORLD
            fx.walk(named[a.arg].body)
            frame.env[a.arg] = union(fx.returns) | WORLD if fx.returns else WORLD
            if any(r.resp is not None for r in fx.returns):
                frame.env[a.arg] = union(fx.returns)
        else:
            frame.env[a.arg] = WORLD
    if chain:
        frame.env["self"] = WORLD
    run.asserts.clear()             # a fixture's asserts are its own preconditions
    frame.walk(func.body)
    if not run.reads:
        return None
    if not run.v2_seen:
        unknown = [r for r in run.reads if r[3] is None]
        if not unknown:
            return None
        r = unknown[0]
        what = "path" if r[4] == "client" else "URL"
        return ("undecided", f"undecided: a {r[1]} whose {what} is not read (`{r[2]}`), and no "
                "v2 read seen", [])
    verdict = _verdict(run)
    return verdict + (unpressed(run),)


def unpressed(run):
    """The v2 controls an assert says are drawn whose route the test never requests (C2288's
    shape: Set value… drawn, never pressed). Not judged where a browser drives the page (a
    click names no route) or a request's path is not read (it may be the press)."""
    if any(r[4] == "browser" for r in run.reads) or any(r[3] is None for r in run.reads):
        return []
    requested = {r[2].split("?", 1)[0] for r in run.reads}
    out = []
    for path, where in run.drawn:
        base = path.split("?", 1)[0]
        if UNKNOWN not in base and base not in requested and (path, where) not in out:
            out.append((path, where))
    return out


def _verdict(run):
    first = run.reads[0][0]
    asserts = [a for a in run.asserts if a[0] > first]
    for p_time, what in run.presses:
        for t_time, where in run.traps:
            if t_time < p_time:
                return ("pressing", f"{what}, with a stand-in that fails when called ({where}) "
                        "asserting its effect")
        for a_time, parts, line in asserts:
            if a_time <= p_time:
                continue
            for kind, resp in parts:
                if kind in ("state", "mixed") or (kind in ("response",) and resp is not None
                                                   and resp > p_time):
                    return ("pressing", f"{what}, then {line} asserts the effect "
                            f"({kind}{', read after the press' if kind == 'response' else ''})")
    state = [a for a in asserts if any(k == "state" for k, _r in a[1])]
    if state:
        return ("state", f"asserts state at {state[0][2]} without pressing a control")
    if run.unread:
        return ("undecided", "undecided: " + run.unread[0])
    v2 = next(r for r in run.reads if r[3])
    where = f"{v2[1]} {v2[2]}"
    kinds = [k for _t, parts, _l in asserts for k, _r in parts if k != "trivial"]
    if not kinds:
        return ("presence", f"asserts nothing after its read ({where})")
    if run.presses:
        return ("presence", f"presses ({run.presses[0][1]}) but asserts only its own answer, "
                "never the effect")
    if all(k == "status" for k in kinds):
        return ("presence", f"status only: {len(kinds)} assert(s) on {where}'s status")
    return ("presence", f"draws only: {len(kinds)} assert(s) on what {where} drew")


def inventory(root, controls=None):
    """{test id: (verdict, reason)} over every UI test under *root*/tests, and the count of
    test functions parsed; *controls*, a dict, is given {test id: [(path, where)]} of the
    controls each asserts drawn and never requests."""
    for cache in (FileFacts._cache, _INFOS, _RETURNS, S._PARSED, S._MODULE_CACHE):
        cache.clear()           # each scan reads the files as they are now
    out, parsed = {}, 0
    for path in S.test_files(root):
        facts = FileFacts.of(root, path)
        if facts is None:
            continue
        rp = S.rel(root, path)
        for chain, classes, func in S.iter_tests(facts.tree):
            parsed += 1
            got = judge(root, facts, chain, classes, func)
            if got is not None:
                tid = "::".join([rp] + chain + [func.name])
                out[tid] = got[:2]
                if got[2] and controls is not None:
                    controls[tid] = got[2]
    return out, parsed


# --- the ratchet file ------------------------------------------------------------------------

HEADER = '''"""Behaviour over presence: the UI tests that assert only presence, and those the parse
cannot decide (board TI, item 4; decision D5, docs/TEST_INTEGRITY.md). Generated by
`scripts/nmas-presence-inventory --write`, which states the property; held by
tests/test_presence_only.py and declared `shrinks` in tests/ratchet_lists.py.

Each listed test is converted to press its control and assert the effect, and then leaves the
list (a converted test still listed fails the test). A new presence-only test is not added: it
is written to press. (Not a test module.)
"""
'''


def render(found):
    def block(comment, name, ids):
        if not ids:
            return "\n".join([comment, f"{name} = frozenset()"])
        return "\n".join([comment, f"{name} = frozenset({{"] +
                         [f'    "{i}",' for i in sorted(ids)] + ["})"])
    presence = [i for i, (v, _r) in found.items() if v == "presence"]
    undecided = [i for i, (v, _r) in found.items() if v == "undecided"]
    return (HEADER + "\n" +
            block("# The UI tests that assert only presence. Only shrinks: a test converted to "
                  "press\n# its control and assert the effect leaves.", "PRESENCE_ONLY", presence)
            + "\n\n" +
            block("# The UI tests the parse cannot decide, each for the reason the script "
                  "prints.\n# Only shrinks: one made readable, or converted, leaves.",
                  "UNDECIDED", undecided)
            + "\n")


def report(found, parsed, show_all=False, controls=None, show_controls=False):
    lines = []
    order = ("presence", "undecided") + (("pressing", "state") if show_all else ())
    for verdict in order:
        for tid in sorted(t for t, (v, _r) in found.items() if v == verdict):
            lines.append(f"{verdict}\t{tid}\t{S.public(found[tid][1])}")
    controls = controls or {}
    if show_controls:
        for tid in sorted(controls):
            for path, where in controls[tid]:
                lines.append(f"drawn-unpressed\t{tid}\t{found[tid][0]}; asserts {path} drawn "
                             f"({where}), never requests it")
    counts = collections.Counter(v for v, _r in found.values())
    lines.append("")
    lines.append(f"# UI tests scanned\t{len(found)}")
    for verdict in ("presence", "undecided", "pressing", "state"):
        lines.append(f"# {verdict}\t{counts.get(verdict, 0)}")
    pressing = sum(1 for t in controls if found[t][0] == "pressing")
    lines.append(f"# tests asserting a v2 control drawn that they never request\t{len(controls)}"
                 f"\t({pressing} of them pressing another control)")
    lines.append(f"# test functions parsed\t{parsed}")
    return lines


def main(argv=None):
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description="Behaviour over presence: the inventory.")
    ap.add_argument("--root", default=REPO, help="the folder holding tests/ (default: this "
                    "repository)")
    ap.add_argument("--all", action="store_true", help="list the pressing and state tests too")
    ap.add_argument("--controls", action="store_true",
                    help="list each v2 control a test asserts drawn and never requests")
    ap.add_argument("--write", action="store_true",
                    help="write the presence and undecided ids into tests/presence_only.py")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    root = os.path.abspath(a.root)
    if not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(root, "tests")):
        print(f"nmas-presence-inventory: {root} holds no tests/ folder", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    controls = {}
    found, parsed = inventory(root, controls)
    sys.stdout.write("\n".join(report(found, parsed, a.all, controls, a.controls)) + "\n")
    if a.write:
        dest = os.path.join(root, "tests", "presence_only.py")
        with open(dest, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(render(found))
        print(f"# written\t{os.path.relpath(dest, root)}")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
